Maya (Presales): Heads-up
Customer kickoff Thurs AM. They asked for a 1-page POC runbook: minimal streaming SDK examples (Node + Go), function/tool-call pattern, structured JSON output validation, quick handshake cURL, and a short security QA (KMS, retention, SOC2 contact). Can someone assemble a compact draft by EOD?

Diego (Eng): Ill take the draft. Clarify: Hosted EU region, ephemeral creds required, and want an explicit fallback to a quantized variant for cost spikes?

Lina (Sales): Correct: hosted (eu-west). Theyll want ephemeral creds example + a lightweight cost fallback. They also asked for a note about logs: default not retained; can enable with consent.

Maya (Presales): Yes to ephemeral creds + consented logs only. Include suggested batching knobs and a fallback routing policy. Keep the commercial pricing as placeholders 
(finance will supplant).

Diego (Eng): Draft runbook text (one-paragraph bullets + inline snippets):

- Quick objective: Demo streaming chat with function/tool calls and structured output validation. Show how to route to cheaper model when GPU pool saturated.
- Environment: Hosted (eu), model: r-infer-2 (fallback: r-infer-2-quant-small).
- Auth: API key or short-lived token (example below), KMS for keys; TLS mandatory.

Node snippet (stream + function call):

```js
// Node: streaming + toolcall
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY, region: 'eu' });
const s = client.chat.stream({ model: 'r-infer-2' });
s.on('event', e => {
  if (e.type === 'function_call') {
    // call out to tool
    fetch('https://hooks.customer/call', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(e.payload) });
  }
  if (e.type === 'message') console.log(JSON.stringify(e.message));
});
```

Go snippet (stream + simple schema validation):

```go
// Go: basic stream receive
cli := redwood.NewClient(os.Getenv("RW_KEY"))
stream := cli.ChatStream(context.Background(), redwood.ChatParams{Model: "r-infer-2"})
for ev := range stream.Events() {
  switch ev.Type {
  case redwood.EventFunctionCall:
    // tool call
    http.Post("https://hooks.customer/call", "application/json", bytes.NewReader(ev.Payload))
  case redwood.EventMessage:
    // validate structured output (example)
    // validateJSON(ev.Message, expectedSchema)
  }
}
```

Handshake cURL (SSE style):

```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $RW_KEY" \
  -H "Accept: text/event-stream" \
  "https://api.redwood.ai/v1/streams/chat?model=r-infer-2&region=eu"
```

Diego (Eng): Structured output: recommend a compact JSON Schema example consumers can validate against on receive: "{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"intent\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"items\":{\"type\":\"array\"}}}". Also mention SDK hook for schema validation + checksum.

Diego (Eng): Operational knobs: set batching window 10-25ms, enable KV prefix caching, enable model quantization for fallback. Fallback policy: if queuing latency > 80ms or GPU queue > 75% -> route to r-infer-2-quant-small same region.

Lina (Sales): Pricing blurb (placeholder): two options: 1) Reserved capacity (commit + burst bucket) — better unit cost; 2) Pay-as-you-go hosted for pilots. Show example rows but mark as "TBD by finance".

Maya (Presales): Security QA checklist (short bullets):
- Data residency: EU-only endpoints; VPC option for Private deploy.
- Encryption: TLS in transit; KMS-managed keys at rest. HSM optional.
- Logs: not stored by default; retention policy configurable; customer can opt-out.
- Access control: short-lived tokens + RBAC; IP allowlist for onprem bridges.
- Incident response: contact secops@redwood.ai; standard IR SLA and post-incident report available.

legal-bot: Add: include SOC2 attestation link and DPA pointer.

Maya (Presales): Great. Two small asks: add quick troubleshooting bullets (auth 401 -> check time sync/clock for ephemeral tokens; SSE handshake stalls -> missing Accept header/CORS; function calls failing -> webhook TLS mismatch or IP block). And flag any enterprise blockers: SSO/SAML for onprem, dedicated GPU capacity timeline (2-4 weeks provisioning), and KMS integration details.

Diego (Eng): Adding troubleshooting snips now.

Lina (Sales): I'll chase finance and legal for the placeholder fields and SOC2 doc.

Maya (Presales): Please tag me when final. I'll paste the 1-page summary into the customer drive and attach the runbook. Thanks team. :rocket:
